L675: **BMJ Open**
L676: **MATERIALS AND METHODS**
L677: A systematic review of peer-reviewed literature relating to the effect of RET and vitamin D3 supplementation
L678: on musculoskeletal health in older adults was conducted in accordance with a study protocol registered on the
L679: PROSPERO database (record number CRD42015020157). The protocol was informed by the Cochrane
L680: Handbook for Systematic Reviews of Interventions[25], and reporting conformed to the Preferred Reporting
L681: Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-analysis (PRISMA) statement[26].
L682: **Eligibility Criteria**
L683: Randomized controlled trials were sought for this study. Journal studies included: (1) male and/or female
L684: participants (aged ≥65 years or mean age ≥ 65 years) (2) enlisted RET and vitamin D3 supplementation (studies
L685: utilising vitamin D3 and calcium supplementation were included) (3) included measures of muscle strength,
L686: function, muscle power, body composition, serum vitamin D/calcium status or quality of life (4) compared
L687: results with a control group (sedentary/usual care/no vitamin D3 supplementation). Articles were excluded if
L688: participants were supplemented with additional protein or any supplement/medication with a known anabolic
L689: effect on muscle tissue.
L690: **Search methods for identification of studies**
L691: Articles published before March 2016 were included. A computerised search of Science Direct, MedLine,
L692: PubMed, Google Scholar and Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials (Cochrane CENTRAL accessed by
L693: Wiley Science) databases was conducted. Table 1 shows the Medline search strategy, devised by AEA and LH.
L694: **Data items and collection**
L695: Data were extracted independently by 2 reviewers (AEA and ASA) using a standardised data extraction sheet;
L696: any disagreements were discussed and resolved with a third person (CAG). The inter-rater reliability was
L697: assessed using Cohen’s Kappa[27]. Data items including general information, participant characteristics and
L698: details of the intervention were extracted. For key outcomes the definition used by the authors, methodology,
L699: results, mean differences and the presence/absence of statistical significance were reported.
