L1227: **BMJ Open**
L1228: **Risk of bias within studies**
L1229: For all studies, a high proportion of components were assigned an unclear risk of bias due to insufficient
L1230: information and the unknown effect on study outcome measures. Many studies reported insufficient
L1231: information on concealment and blinding procedures, or whether procedures were in place in the event of
L1232: unblinding. In total, 6 studies were judged to have an unclear risk of bias[21,31-33,35,36]. Component 1 was
L1233: assessed as having a low risk of bias for all studies. 1 study was assessed as having an overall high risk of
L1234: bias[34] due to component 5, as no data were entered into the analyses for participants with missing data.
L1235: **GRADE analysis**
L1236: The GRADE summary of findings table for groups 1 and 2 are shown in Tables 5 and 6.
L1237: Within group 1, all studies were evaluated as moderate quality of evidence; no serious risk of bias was
L1238: detected. Due to the nature of the studies included within this review, no serious indirectness was detected;
L1239: all outcomes were measured directly without the use of a surrogate. Publication bias was not detected, and
L1240: due to the number of studies included, it was not possible to produce funnel plots for any outcomes. Reasons
L1241: for downgrading the quality of evidence included serious inconsistency due to substantial heterogeneity, and
L1242: serious imprecision due to confidence intervals crossing the line of no effect.
L1243: Within group 2 studies, 5 outcomes were graded as high to moderate quality of evidence (SPPB, TUG, muscle
L1244: strength of the lower limb, hand grip strength and BMD of the hip). Remaining outcomes were graded as low
L1245: or very low quality, meaning that one could have little or very little confidence in the effect estimate. Common
L1246: reasons for downgrading outcomes included a combination of serious risk of bias (due to the inclusion of
L1247: study[34]), serious imprecision or serious inconsistency.
L1248: **Results of individual studies and synthesis of results**
L1249: Results of the 2 groups of studies are reported separately. Within each group, there were outcomes unsuitable
L1250: for quantitative synthesis, due to a lack of studies with common outcomes or aspects of studies too dissimilar
L1251: for comparison; therefore, a narrative analysis was utilised.
L1252: **Quantitative synthesis**
L1253: Outcomes compared for group 1 included muscle strength of the lower limb, TUG and BMD of the hip and
L1254: spine (Figures 2-5). Only muscle strength of the lower limb was found to be significant, with a large effect size
L1255: in favour of the intervention group (2.69, 95% CI 0.95, 4.42. _p_ = 0.002).
