L3460: **BMJ Open**
L3461: **MATERIALS AND METHODS**
L3462: A systematic review of peer-reviewed literature relating to the effect of RET and vitamin D3 supplementation
L3463: on musculoskeletal health in older adults was conducted in accordance with a study protocol registered on the
L3464: PROSPERO database (record number CRD42015020157). The protocol was informed by the Cochrane
L3465: Handbook for Systematic Reviews of Interventions[25], and reporting conformed to the Preferred Reporting
L3466: Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-analysis (PRISMA) statement[26].
L3467: **Eligibility Criteria**
L3468: Randomized controlled trials were sought for this study. Journal studies included: (1) male and/or female
L3469: participants (aged ≥65 years or mean age ≥ 65 years) (2) enlisted RET and vitamin D3 supplementation (studies
L3470: utilising vitamin D3 and calcium supplementation were included) (3) included measures of muscle strength,
L3471: function, muscle power, body composition, serum vitamin D/calcium status or quality of life (4) compared
L3472: results with a control group (sedentary/usual care/no vitamin D3 supplementation). Articles were excluded if
L3473: participants were supplemented with additional protein or any supplement/medication with a known anabolic
L3474: effect on muscle tissue.
L3475: **Search methods for identification of studies**
L3476: Articles published before March 2016 were included. A computerised search of Science Direct, MedLine,
L3477: PubMed, Google Scholar and Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials (Cochrane CENTRAL accessed by
L3478: Wiley Science) databases was conducted. Table 1 shows the Medline search strategy, devised by AEA and LH.
