L3817: **BMJ Open**
L3818: **Study demographics**
L3819: 7 eligible studies included a total of 792 participants of mean age 72.8 years (Table 2). Of these, 1 included
L3820: only males[31] and 3 included only females[21,35,36]. All studies included healthy participants living
L3821: independently, except for 2 studies; [35] included participants living within a retirement community and [36]
L3822: included institutionalized participants living in nursing homes, service flats or cloistered communities.
L3823: **Interventions**
L3824: Studies assigned to group 1 included Agergaard et al., 2015[31]; Bunout et al., 2006[32] and Uusi-Rasi et al.,
L3825: 2015[21]. In group 1, all participants took part in RET; incorporating a warm-up and strengthening exercises
L3826: utilising commercial weight machines[21,31] or Thera-bands[31]. 2 studies included balance challenging
L3827: aspects[21,32]. All studies included supervised, progressive exercise sessions; progression was monitored by a
L3828: 5 rep max (RM) test[31], Borg scale[32] or metabolic equivalents (METs)[21]. Total number of sessions
L3829: delivered ranged from 36[31]to 156[21], over a duration of 16 weeks[31] to 24 months[21]. All administered a
L3830: vitamin D3 supplement, orally in tablet form; doses ranged from 400IU [32] to 1920 IU[31] per day; in 2 studies
L3831: participants were supplemented with 800mg calcium per day[31,32] and 1 study supplemented the control
L3832: group with a placebo[21].
L3833: 6 studies assigned to group 2 included; Bunout et al., 2006[32], Drey et al., 2011[33] Gianoudis et al., 2014[34],
L3834: Jessup et al., 2003[35], Uusi-Rasi et al., 2015[21] and Verschueren et al., 2011[36]. Within group 2, all
L3835: participants took a vitamin D3 supplement, orally in tablet form. Doses ranged from 400 IU[32,35] to 2000
L3836: IU[33] per day; 1 study monitored serum 25(OH)D at baseline to determine supplement dosage[33]. In 4
L3837: studies[32,34-36] all participants were supplemented with calcium; doses ranged from 700mg[34] to
L3838: 1000mg[35,36] per day. The intervention group took part in RET. Studies utilised machine weights and
L3839: pulleys[21,33-35], Thera-bands[32], weighted vests[35] and Whole Body Vibration (WBV) machines[36] for
L3840: resistance. 5 studies included balance challenging aspects[21,32-35]. All studies employed supervised,
L3841: progressive exercise sessions monitored via a Borg scale[32-34], addition of weights to weighted vests[35],
L3842: estimation of METs or individual ability[36]. Total number of sessions delivered ranged from 24[33] to 156[21],
L3843: over a duration of 12 weeks[33] to 24 months[21]. Note that 2 studies included comparators which allowed
L3844: allocation to both groups [21,32].
