L4015: - Risk of bias domains of assessment. 1: Random sequence generation, 2: Allocation concealment,
L4016: 3: Blinding of participants and personnel, 4: Blinding of outcome assessment, 5: Incomplete outcome
L4017: data, 6: Selective reporting, 7: Other sources of bias. Judgements possible: H – High risk of bias, U –
L4018: Unclear risk of bias, L – Low risk of bias
L4019: **For peer review only - http://bmjopen.bmj.com/site/about/guidelines.xhtml**
L4020: **Risk of bias within studies**
L4021: The risk of bias analyses are displayed within Table 4. For all studies, a high proportion of components were
L4022: assigned an unclear risk of bias due to insufficient information and the unknown effect on study outcome
L4023: measures. Many studies reported insufficient information on concealment and blinding procedures, or
L4024: whether procedures were in place in the event of unblinding. In total, 6 studies were judged to have an
L4025: unclear risk of bias[21,31-33,35,36]. Component 1 was assessed as having a low risk of bias for all studies. 1
L4026: study was assessed as having an overall high risk of bias[34] due to component 5, as no data were entered into
L4027: the analyses for participants with missing data.
