L4633: For group 2 secondary outcomes, small and non-significant gains in appendicular lean mass were
L4634: demonstrated in the intervention group of study[33]. In study[36], muscle mass of the upper limb decreased
L4635: non-significantly in both the intervention and control groups, although to a lesser extent in the intervention
L4636: group. BMD of the femoral neck was gained in both groups, although by a higher percentage in the control
L4637: group; both trends were non-significant.
